WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.700
Let's go next to our call or from the two,
six, seven area code.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.660
Who's calling today from two, six, seven.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:10.099
Oh, hi David.

00:00:10.099 --> 00:00:12.009
Can you hear me?

00:00:12.009 --> 00:00:13.450
Yes, I can.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:14.450
Who's this?

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:18.090
Uh, my name is, uh, Tony Holland.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.090
All right.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.750
Tell me what's going on.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:21.750
Phil Philly.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.030
All right, very good.

00:00:23.030 --> 00:00:29.340
Um, well I wanted to talk about, uh, reparations
and how I just don't pretty much agree or

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:32.680
I'm not really hearing any realistic.

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:34.570
Uh, I don't know.

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:38.890
I just don't agree with the way that the conversation
is taking place, even from, uh, you know,

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.410
my, uh, my fellow black people.

00:00:40.410 --> 00:00:43.670
Um, so here's a stance really quick, real
rundown.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:49.880
It's all about slavery, Jim Crow, segregation,
red lining.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:53.829
Uh, we all know those kinds of things that
we're very well versed in.

00:00:53.829 --> 00:01:00.140
How I, what I feel is that, um, uh, white
America has a standard response for that,

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:07.130
which is, uh, we are going, uh, maintain,
uh, the white supremacist system that is in

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:13.450
place by saying that all of those people are
dead and we cannot be held responsible.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:19.040
And I just don't feel that as a community
we have formed a proper response to that.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:23.999
Uh, so for me, I look at it economically,
black people owned 2% of businesses in the

00:01:23.999 --> 00:01:30.789
United States of America, meaning that, uh,
almost a hundred percent of us have to leave

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:34.729
our community to have access to a single opportunity
in this country.

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:37.340
A defining our largest issue.

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:41.000
Uh, the root of our issue is in fact labor
dependent.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:46.439
Uh, the, the, you know, we have about six
and a half million black men, over 2 million

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.380
black women with felony convictions.

00:01:48.380 --> 00:01:54.740
And the statistics bear out that there is
a one 10th of a percent of a chance at ever

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:58.719
being gainfully employed again if you are
black with a felony conviction.

00:01:58.719 --> 00:01:59.719
Right.

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:05.310
So my whole, my whole thing is, one, I don't
support cash payments whatsoever because there

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:07.169
is no reason.

00:02:07.169 --> 00:02:09.310
I just do not see a successful path.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:14.560
If you were to give a bunch of people money
who have no financial savvy about themselves,

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:16.610
then it's just going to be a waste of money.

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:22.670
So for that I agree with, but I support a
comprehensive reparations package that, uh,

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:30.019
that, you know, similar to what Maryanne Williamson
says, I advocate elite $250 billion paid in

00:02:30.019 --> 00:02:37.480
$25 billion yearly increments all for the
purposes of, uh, of establishing and growing

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:42.579
black owned businesses and labor dependence
by 50% in a 10 year period.

00:02:42.579 --> 00:02:43.579
Yeah.

00:02:43.579 --> 00:02:47.159
So listen, basically, I mean it sounds like
you and I are on a pretty similar page.

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:52.640
So I, this actually came up in my conversation
with Sam Harris about a month ago where, uh,

00:02:52.640 --> 00:03:03.189
yeah, basically I think that a focus on reparations
in the democratic primary may be counterproductive

00:03:03.189 --> 00:03:08.359
to ultimately getting someone to unseat Trump
as a merely practical matter.

00:03:08.359 --> 00:03:14.629
That being said, I am very open to the way,
uh, to, to doing reparations.

00:03:14.629 --> 00:03:18.769
In a way that is not just throwing cash at
people because that will help some people

00:03:18.769 --> 00:03:23.430
to some degree, but it's not going to change
really what we're trying to change at its

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.430
core.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.579
So what, what the idea that I like and I am
open to different ways of doing it in terms

00:03:28.579 --> 00:03:35.569
of the numbers, is to spend the money in ways
where we're going to boost minority homeownership.

00:03:35.569 --> 00:03:41.870
We're going to boost minority entrepreneurship,
we're going to fund education and to start

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:49.750
trying to level out what are the remaining
inequalities of horrible historical realities

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.750
in the United States.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:53.060
So it sounds like you and I are sort of on
similar pages.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.349
Um, yeah.

00:03:54.349 --> 00:03:58.209
I mean, yeah, except one point.

00:03:58.209 --> 00:04:07.060
Um, I honestly take offense to you saying
that, um, you feel that, uh, basically we'll

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:12.110
lose and submit the election to Donald Trump
if we actually, for once in this country,

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:16.660
try and represent, represent black people
at the point of their most pressing needs.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:20.080
Well, it's not a question of taking a, I mean,
it's not a question of taking offense.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:23.030
You could, you could argue that I'm wrong
about it or that I'm

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.110
well, well let, let me finish my point.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:28.110
Yeah.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:32.110
Um, I just feel like what is being presented
is people aren't really thinking outside the

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:33.120
box for me.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:39.860
I don't see an issue with the democratic party,
uh, uh, potentially, uh, losing if they just

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:42.080
centered their message around appealing to
the race.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:43.290
Let me make sure, hold on.

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:44.910
Let me make sure I understand what you're
saying.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.580
I want to make sure I understand what you're
saying.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:52.210
When you say you don't see an issue, are you
saying you don't think Democrats will lose

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.380
or you don't care if they lose by focusing?

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.250
I just want to make sure I'm understanding
what you're saying.

00:04:57.250 --> 00:04:58.250
Do not.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:04:59.250
Okay.

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.330
What I am saying is I do not think that that
is the reality.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:07.870
I think that that is the expression of a fear
of the people who haven't really thought about

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.210
it beyond a typical talking.

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:11.210
You're right.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:17.280
And I think here's the important thing to
keep in mind when I say I see it as electorally

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.280
risky.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:23.170
The conversation you and I are having and
the way you and I would go about this I don't

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:27.020
think is the risky conversation, which is
to deal with things like home ownership and

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:28.570
education entrepreneurship.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:34.280
The problem is that whenever it comes up,
the conversation becomes one of how do you

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:38.080
decide who we give cash to and how much do
we give them?

00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:41.160
And you and I both agree that [inaudible]
the wrong conversation and I don't see them

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:43.180
having a conversation that's different than
that one.

00:05:43.180 --> 00:05:47.150
That being said, if the conversation they
have is the one you're having, I'm all for

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.150
it.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:53.940
Well, well there's, I think we need to reorient
a discussion and get away from the concept

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.280
of cash payments in general.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:58.600
I think that is the single biggest thing that
holds us back.

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:03.680
I think the second biggest thing is the assumption
that we cannot run on reparations.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:10.420
And when, uh, one of the, one of the things
that I keep in mind is actually shopping a

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:16.750
reparations package to uh, actually racist
and, and people that are connected to a hate

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.490
group such as the KKK.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:23.840
And what I would say to them was, do you want
less black people working and your place of

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:24.840
employment?

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:27.950
Do you want less black children, you know,
going to school with your white children.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:33.010
Let me, let me finish before you, before you
say this and do you, uh, over here respond

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:35.930
and do you want less black people living in
your neighborhood?

00:06:35.930 --> 00:06:41.530
Well, if you support a comprehensive reparations
package, what we will do is what it will do

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:45.900
is allow for the black community to be self
sufficient and they're going to most likely

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:50.810
stay in Bay area when 100% of them don't have
to leave for opportunities.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.580
All right, let me think more about that part.

00:06:52.580 --> 00:06:54.280
I have not given that part thought.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:55.410
I appreciate the call.

00:06:55.410 --> 00:06:59.790
I do want to get to a couple more people,
but I, you've, you've very well explained

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:02.280
your position and I appreciate it.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.830
Thank you David.

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:04.920
I really appreciate your time.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:07.030
You have to do a fantastic show.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:11.660
Uh, I came across you a few months ago, maybe
about three months ago, and I don't agree

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:16.280
with everything you say, but I, it's just
everything about your presentation, the way

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.840
you speak, the way you present your ideas
appeals to me.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:22.800
I have listened to the young Turks for five
years, never became a contributor.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.700
I became a contributor of yours within the
first week.

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:26.780
Thank you.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.780
Appreciate it.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:28.780
All right, very good.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:29.780
Good to hear from Tony from Philly.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:30.120
Hope to hear from you again.

